{
  "id": "l05",
  "number": 5,
  "chapter": 1,
  "title": "The Dative Case",
  "subtitle": "For, to (purpose & recipient) · -āya, -ssa (singular) and -ānaṃ (plural)",
  "tags": [
    "New",
    "Cases"
  ],
  "minutes": 14,
  "revision": {
    "title": "Quick Revision — Lessons I–IV",
    "summaryHtml": "You've mastered four cases: <strong>Nominative</strong> (subject), <strong>Accusative</strong> (object), <strong>Instrumental</strong> (by/with), and <strong>Ablative</strong> (from). You're halfway through the case system!",
    "connectionHtml": "<strong>Connection:</strong> The Ablative tells us <em>from</em> where. The Dative tells us <em>for whom</em> or <em>to whom</em>. \"He brings rice <em>for</em> the monk.\"",
    "questions": [
      {
        "q": "What are the three Ablative singular endings?",
        "a": "<strong>-ā, -smā, -mhā</strong>"
      },
      {
        "q": "\"The child falls from the palace\" → Pāli?",
        "a": "<strong>Dārako pāsādā patati</strong>"
      },
      {
        "q": "Which two cases share the plural ending -ehi?",
        "a": "<strong>Instrumental</strong> and <strong>Ablative</strong>"
      }
    ]
  },
  "teach": [
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "title": "The Dative CasePurpose & Recipient",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "eyebrow": "Grammar",
          "html": "The <em>Dative</em> Case<br>Purpose &amp; Recipient"
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "html": "The Dative case indicates the <strong>indirect object</strong> — the person <em>for whom</em> or <em>to whom</em> something is done. It also marks <strong>purpose</strong>."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "html": "Dative answers: <strong>For whom?</strong> / <strong>To whom?</strong> / <strong>For what purpose?</strong>"
        },
        {
          "type": "rule",
          "title": "For masculine nouns ending in -a:",
          "formulas": [
            "Singular: base + <em>-āya</em> or <em>-ssa</em>",
            "Plural:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;base + <em>-ānaṃ</em>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "caption": "Cases learned so far",
          "head": [
            "Case",
            "Function",
            "Singular",
            "Plural"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Nominative",
              "Subject",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-o</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ā</span>"
            ],
            [
              "Accusative",
              "Object",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ṃ</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-e</span>"
            ],
            [
              "Instrumental",
              "By/with",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ena</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ehi</span>"
            ],
            [
              "Ablative",
              "From",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ā/-smā/-mhā</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ehi</span>"
            ],
            [
              "Dative",
              "For/to",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-āya / -ssa</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ānaṃ</span>"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
